# Cypress tests (Fernly)

## 1. Queries

Prefer `findByRole`, then `findByLabelText`, then `findByText`. Never target CSS modules or tag names.

```tsx
// Good — QuantityStepper.cy.tsx
cy.findByRole('button', { name: 'Increase quantity' }).click();

// Bad
cy.get('.button').last().click();
cy.get('button').contains('+').click();
```

## 2. States

Assert disabled, checked, or values with `.then(($el) => expect($el, 'label').to.be.disabled)`. A failing `.should()` on `findByRole` reports "Unable to find" when the locator exists but the state is wrong.

```tsx
// Good
cy.findByRole('button', { name: 'Increase quantity' }).then(($btn) => {
  expect($btn, '+ at stock limit').to.be.disabled;
});

// Bad — QuantityStepper.cy.tsx (misleading failure when + is wrongly enabled)
cy.findByRole('button', { name: 'Increase quantity' }).should('be.disabled');
```

## 3. Waiting

Never `cy.wait(<milliseconds>)`. Wait on an intercept alias or on what the user sees.

```tsx
// Good — UI test
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants*', { fixture: 'plants/browse-positive.json' }).as('plants');
cy.visit('/');
cy.wait('@plants');
cy.findByRole('heading', { name: /plants/i });

// Bad
cy.visit('/');
cy.wait(500);
```

## 4. Data

Component tests pass props in the mount; UI tests load API bodies from `web/cypress/fixtures/` — one file per scenario (positive, negative, edge).

```tsx
// Good — component
cy.mount(<QuantityStepper value={3} max={3} onChange={cy.spy()} />);

// Good — UI
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants/pl-monstera', { fixture: 'plants/pl-monstera-not-found.json' });

// Bad — inline API body in the spec
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants', { statusCode: 500, body: { detail: 'boom' } });
```

## 5. Mocks

`cy.intercept` only `/api/*` requests, with an alias. Never stub the page bundle or `cy.stub` the router.

```tsx
// Good
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/cart', { fixture: 'cart/signed-in.json' }).as('cart');

// Bad
cy.intercept('GET', '/src/pages/BrowsePage.tsx', { statusCode: 200, body: '...' });
```

## 6. Tags

Exactly one level tag per test: `{ tags: '@component' }` or `{ tags: '@ui' }`.

```tsx
// Good
it('disables + at the stock limit', { tags: '@component' }, () => { /* ... */ });

// Bad — no tag, or two level tags on one test
it('disables + at the stock limit', () => { /* ... */ });
it('disables − at the minimum', { tags: ['@component', '@ui'] }, () => { /* ... */ });
```

## 7. App code

Do not change `web/src` to green a test. If the test matches `docs/PRODUCT.md` and the app fails, record it in `FINDINGS.md` (see F-01: stepper at stock limit).

```tsx
// Good — failing test + FINDINGS.md F-01, fix suggested in findings not in QuantityStepper.tsx

// Bad — patch web/src/components/QuantityStepper.tsx so value > max becomes value >= max without a finding
```

## 8. Evidence

Label what you actually did: **executed** (test run), **inspected** (code/DOM only), or **not yet tested**. Do not call a suspicion a finding without a failing test or exact steps.

```markdown
<!-- Good — FINDINGS.md F-01 -->
- **Evidence:** `web/cypress/component/QuantityStepper.cy.tsx` — test **disables + at the stock limit** (fails: + is enabled when `value={3}` and `max={3}`).

<!-- Bad -->
- **Evidence:** The + button is probably broken at max quantity.
```
